<title>UK: Europe beet areas see differing moisture levels.</title>
<headline>Europe beet areas see differing moisture levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moisture levels in Italian and Spanish sugar beet areas improved in the last week but soils in France and eastern Germany were suffering from a shortage of rain, F.O. Licht said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In its daily report, Licht said rains had continued to improve low soil moisture supplies in Italy and considerably exceed normal levels in Spain where yields were on the increase.</p>
<p>West European sugar beet areas reported rains of between six and 25 mm in nearly all locations during the week ended June 10, it said.</p>
<p>But the main area of concern was eastern Germany  where rains well below normal levels had led to moisture shortages in nearly half of the sugar beet area.</p>
<p>&quot;Also in France it could be getting too dry. However, rains are expected to increase which could avert moisture stress,&quot; Licht said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
